 IMMUTABLE & MUTABLE INFRASTRUCTURE : 

    Immutable infrastructure means that once a resource is created, it cannot be modified. If changes are needed, a new resource is created and the old one is destroyed.

    Mutable infrastructure allows resources to be modified after creation.

    Terraform promotes immutable infrastructure by encouraging the use of declarative configurations and version control.

  IDEMPOTENT : 

    Idempotent means that applying the same configuration multiple times will result in the same state. Terraform ensures that the desired state is achieved regardless of how many times the configuration is applied.         

