15. COMMON ERRORS
====================================================================

ERROR 1:

Invalid for_each argument

REASON:

The map keys or set values are not known at plan time.

SOLUTION:

Make the instance keys known before Terraform creates
the resources.

ERROR 2:

Sensitive value used in for_each

REASON:

Terraform cannot expose sensitive values as instance keys.

SOLUTION:

Use non-sensitive keys and keep secret values separately.

ERROR 3:

Duplicate map keys

REASON:

A map cannot contain duplicate keys.

SOLUTION:

Use unique keys for every resource instance.

ERROR 4:

Changing for_each key

REASON:

Terraform sees a different resource address.

SOLUTION:

Review the plan carefully. Use a Terraform state move
when you intend to preserve the existing resource.

