17. 60-SECOND INTERVIEW ANSWER
====================================================================

"In Terraform, for_each is a meta-argument that allows us
to create multiple instances of a resource or module using
a map or a set of strings.

For example, in an AWS project, if I need to create S3
buckets for dev, test, and production, I can define those
environments in a map or set and use one resource block
with for_each.

I use each.key to identify the resource and each.value
to access its configuration.

This avoids duplicate code and makes infrastructure
easier to manage. Unlike count, which uses numeric
indexes, for_each uses meaningful keys, making it useful
when resources have different configurations."

